# Third-party notices

This project does not vendor the 47 Python dependencies listed in
`requirements-lock.txt`. For every exact package/version, the verified
license/terms, installed copyright/license-file source, required notice,
bundling status and redistribution assessment are recorded in
`tables/release_audit/dependency_license_inventory.csv` and rendered in
`reports/LICENSE_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX.md`. Those records are incorporated by
reference and must accompany any redistribution that bundles dependencies.

Key upstream components include NumPy, SciPy, pandas, scikit-learn,
Matplotlib, PyArrow, pymatgen, Pillow, Requests and PyYAML. Preserve each
upstream distribution's license when redistributing its binaries or source.
The current source/release candidate does not bundle those distributions.

The four task snapshots derive from Matbench v0.1. Matbench software is MIT
licensed, but individual task data retain upstream provenance and citation
requirements. Matbench and Materials Project software/data terms do not by
themselves establish the author's right to redistribute the locally processed
snapshot files. Raw task snapshots remain excluded even though the author has
authorized publication of the rights-audited original processed outputs.

